1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
This is Postern Browser.
A hardened distribution of Firefox ESR.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,500
The same Gecko engine millions already run —
rebuilt around privacy.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:13,500
Not a new engine. Not Chromium. Firefox ESR,
with the Mozilla branding stripped.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:19,000
Telemetry is gone. No studies, no Pocket,
no crash pings, no phone-home to Mozilla.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Disabled at both the config
and the enterprise-policy level.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,500
resistFingerprinting and letterboxing
present one uniform surface.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:34,000
Timezone reads as UTC. Locale as en-US.
Canvas and audio, spoofed.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,500
This reduces your fingerprint.
It does not erase it.

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:44,500
Strict tracking protection. Dynamic first-party
isolation. HTTPS-only, even in private windows.

10
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,500
WebRTC that won't leak your local IP.
And uBlock Origin, shipped in the box.

11
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,500
Some things break on purpose. That's the trade,
not a bug — DRM is off, and sites may letterbox.

12
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:00,000
We fix compatibility per site,
never by weakening the defense.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,500
Here's the honest part.
Postern Browser makes you harder to track.

14
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:11,000
It does not make you anonymous.
And it has not been independently audited.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,000
For strong anonymity, use the Tor Browser —
the uniformity gold standard.

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,500
Built from public source. Hardened,
not anonymous. Unaudited. Not Tor.

17
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:26,500
Postern Browser. A Postern Labs product.
Public beta.
